---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { internshipMeta, visibleWeeksData, roadmapConfig } from '../data/internshipData.js';
---

<Layout title="Manager Evaluation | SDD Digital Banking" currentPath="/manager-review">
  <div class="container">
    <div style="padding-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      <div class="hero-tag">
        <span>Executive Management & Mentorship</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="hero-title" style="margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
        Manager Review & Evaluation
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
        Review weekly deliverables, adjust weighted performance criteria (100% total), and issue formal milestone sign-offs.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Live Performance Scorecard & Weighted Calculator -->
    <div class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-neutral">SDD Evaluation Metrics</span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-top: 0.35rem;">
            Weighted Evaluation Scorecard
          </h2>
          <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.8125rem; margin-top: 0.2rem;">
            Adjust metric scores (0–100%) to calculate real-time weighted grade.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="text-align: right; background: var(--bg-subtle); padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
          <span style="font-size: 0.6875rem; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 600;">Calculated Grade</span>
          <div style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.2;" id="overall-grade">
            94.0%
          </div>
          <span class="badge badge-success" id="grade-badge">Grade: Outstanding (A)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sliders for each of the 5 criteria -->
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem;">
        {internshipMeta.evaluationCriteria.map((crit, idx) => (
          <div style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 0.85rem;">
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
              <div>
                <strong style="color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 0.84375rem;">{crit.criteria}</strong>
                <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="margin-left: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.65rem;">Weight: {crit.weight}</span>
              </div>
              <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;">
                <span style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-muted);">Score:</span>
                <span class="score-display" id={`score-val-${idx}`} style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); font-family: var(--font-mono); width: 45px; text-align: right; font-size: 0.8125rem;">95%</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.4;">{crit.description}</p>
            <input
              type="range"
              min="0"
              max="100"
              value={idx === 0 ? 100 : idx === 1 ? 95 : idx === 2 ? 90 : idx === 3 ? 95 : 90}
              class="metric-slider"
              data-weight={parseInt(crit.weight)}
              data-index={idx}
              style="width: 100%; accent-color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer;"
            />
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Milestone Sign-Off Table -->
    <div class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Milestone Approval & Sign-Off Register
      </h3>
      <div style="overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);">
        <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.8125rem; text-align: left;">
          <thead>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); background: var(--bg-subtle); color: var(--text-primary);">
              <th style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 500;">Week</th>
              <th style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 500;">Milestone Topic</th>
              <th style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 500;">Target Deliverable</th>
              <th style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 500;">Sign-Off Status</th>
              <th style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 500;">Action</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
              <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--text-primary);">Week 1</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-primary);">Onboarding & Environment Setup</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Verified Local Running Portals</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-success">Approved</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;"><a href="/reports/week-1" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">Report</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); background: var(--bg-subtle);">
              <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent-blue);">Week 2</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 500;">Dual-Portal Architecture & Admin Console</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Pillars 1–8 Checklists &amp; Practice Project</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-warning">Ready for Verification</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;">
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                  <a href="/milestones/week-2/checklists#mentor-rubric" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem; padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;">
                    <span>Mark Practice Project &rarr;</span>
                  </a>
                  <a href="/milestones/week-2" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem; padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;">Plan</a>
                </div>
              </td>
            </tr>
            {visibleWeeksData.slice(2).map((w) => (
              <tr style={`border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); ${w.week === 5 ? 'background: var(--bg-subtle);' : ''}`}>
                <td style={`padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: ${w.week === 5 ? '600' : '500'}; color: ${w.week === 5 ? 'var(--accent-blue)' : 'var(--text-muted)'};`}>Week {w.week}</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 500;">{w.title}</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">{w.deliverable}</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;">
                  {w.week === 5 ? (
                    <span class="badge badge-warning">Day 1 Review Active</span>
                  ) : (
                    <span class="badge badge-neutral">{w.status || 'Scheduled'}</span>
                  )}
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;">
                  {w.week === 5 ? (
                    <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                      <a href="#week-5-day-1-review" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem; padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;">
                        <span>Review Day 1 &darr;</span>
                      </a>
                      <a href="/milestones/week-5/day-1-review" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem; padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;">Full Audit Hub &rarr;</a>
                    </div>
                  ) : (
                    <span style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.75rem;">Upcoming</span>
                  )}
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Week 5, Day 1: Layered Architecture & Serverless Entry — Reviewer Checklist & Intern Submission Audit -->
    <div id="week-5-day-1-review" class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue, #2563eb);">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem;">
        <div>
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
            <span class="badge badge-warning" style="font-size: 0.65rem;">ACTIVE MENTOR REVIEW</span>
            <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-size: 0.65rem;">Week 5 • Day 1 (Nov 2, 2026)</span>
            <span class="badge badge-success" style="font-size: 0.65rem;">Mg Phyo Min Htet: 92/100 (Approved)</span>
            <span class="badge badge-warning" style="font-size: 0.65rem;">Ma Yamin Aye: 62/100 (Needs Revision)</span>
          </div>
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-top: 0.2rem;">
            Week 5, Day 1: Layered Architecture (Controller &rarr; Service &rarr; Repository) &amp; Serverless Entry
          </h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.8125rem; margin-top: 0.2rem; max-width: 840px; line-height: 1.45;">
            Reviewer checklist and codebase ground-truth audit (<code class="code-pill">ibanking17</code> &amp; <code class="code-pill">admin_console</code>) for the Day 1 reports submitted by <strong>Bro Phyo Min Htet</strong> and <strong>Sis Yamin Aye</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center;" class="no-print">
          <a href="/milestones/week-5/day-1-review" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">
            <span>Open Full Day 1 Audit &amp; Diagrams &rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Reviewer Verification Checklist Grid -->
      <div style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.65rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em;">
            Reviewer Checklist Points (Click to Tick)
          </strong>
          <span class="badge badge-neutral" id="mgr-w5-check-counter" style="font-size: 0.7rem;">8 / 8 Verified</span>
        </div>

        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(380px, 1fr)); gap: 0.5rem;">
          <label style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.78125rem; color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer; line-height: 1.4;">
            <input type="checkbox" class="mgr-w5-check" data-key="k1" checked style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
            <span><strong>1. Chat Group Detail Post:</strong> Report posted point-by-point in detail in the chat group.</span>
          </label>
          <label style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.78125rem; color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer; line-height: 1.4;">
            <input type="checkbox" class="mgr-w5-check" data-key="k2" checked style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
            <span><strong>2. Project Structure &amp; Java 17:</strong> Checked <code class="code-pill">pom.xml</code> (Java 17, MSSQL/Postgres JDBC, <code class="code-pill">Sequelize</code>) &amp; <code class="code-pill">Optional</code> vs <code class="code-pill">record</code>/<code class="code-pill">sealed</code>.</span>
          </label>
          <label style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.78125rem; color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer; line-height: 1.4;">
            <input type="checkbox" class="mgr-w5-check" data-key="k3" checked style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
            <span><strong>3. Serverless Endpoint Routing:</strong> Verified <code class="code-pill">@FunctionName</code> &amp; <code class="code-pill">@HttpTrigger</code> HTTP method and route accuracy.</span>
          </label>
          <label style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.78125rem; color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer; line-height: 1.4;">
            <input type="checkbox" class="mgr-w5-check" data-key="k4" checked style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
            <span><strong>4. Dual-Portal Coverage:</strong> Picked 1 true <code class="code-pill">ibanking17</code> endpoint (<code class="code-pill">com.mit.function</code>) &amp; 1 true <code class="code-pill">admin_console</code> endpoint (<code class="code-pill">com.function</code>).</span>
          </label>
          <label style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.78125rem; color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer; line-height: 1.4;">
            <input type="checkbox" class="mgr-w5-check" data-key="k5" checked style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
            <span><strong>5. Auth Context Extraction:</strong> Traced <code class="code-pill">SecurityMiddleware.checkAuth()</code> vs. <code class="code-pill">TokenUtil.isTokenExpired()</code> / <code class="code-pill">ServerUtil.isBTokenAuth()</code>.</span>
          </label>
          <label style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.78125rem; color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer; line-height: 1.4;">
            <input type="checkbox" class="mgr-w5-check" data-key="k6" checked style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
            <span><strong>6. Service Layer &amp; <code class="code-pill">@Transactional</code>:</strong> Identified business rules (OTP, user status, limits) and <code class="code-pill">@Transactional</code> atomicity.</span>
          </label>
          <label style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.78125rem; color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer; line-height: 1.4;">
            <input type="checkbox" class="mgr-w5-check" data-key="k7" checked style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
            <span><strong>7. Repository Layer (<code class="code-pill">Sequelize</code> vs. JDBC):</strong> Inspected <code class="code-pill">Sequelize</code> (<code class="code-pill">findOneSync</code>, <code class="code-pill">createSync</code>) vs raw JDBC <code class="code-pill">PreparedStatement</code> (<code class="code-pill">PayeeDao</code>).</span>
          </label>
          <label style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.78125rem; color: var(--text-primary); cursor: pointer; line-height: 1.4;">
            <input type="checkbox" class="mgr-w5-check" data-key="k8" checked style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
            <span><strong>8. Dependency Chain &amp; Layer Separation Defense:</strong> Mapped <code class="code-pill">Controller &rarr; Service &rarr; DAO</code> and explained why business logic must not sit in Controller/Repo.</span>
          </label>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Side-by-Side Reviewer Verdict Cards -->
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(420px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        <!-- Phyo Min Htet Card -->
        <div style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-top: 3px solid var(--accent-emerald, #10b981); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); padding: 1rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <strong style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-primary);">Mg Phyo Min Htet (2.11.2026)</strong>
            <span class="badge badge-success">Approved • 92 / 100</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0; line-height: 1.45;">
            <strong>Traced Endpoints:</strong> Customer <code class="code-pill">RequestPayeeSetup.java</code> (<code class="code-pill">POST /api/requestpayeesetup</code>) &amp; <code class="code-pill">AddPayee.java</code> (<code class="code-pill">POST /api/addpayee</code>) in <code class="code-pill">ibanking17</code>; Admin <code class="code-pill">ChangePassword.java</code> (<code class="code-pill">GET /api/changepassword</code>) in <code class="code-pill">admin_console</code>.
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; line-height: 1.4;">
            <li><strong>&#10003; Codebase Accuracy:</strong> Spotted that <code class="code-pill">PayeeDao</code> uses raw JDBC <code class="code-pill">PreparedStatement</code> while <code class="code-pill">UserDao</code>/<code class="code-pill">UserHistoryDao</code> use <code class="code-pill">Sequelize</code> (<code class="code-pill">findOneSync</code>, <code class="code-pill">createSync</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>&#10003; Architecture Critique:</strong> Identified real layer violations where <code class="code-pill">RequestPayeeSetup</code> and <code class="code-pill">AddPayee</code> call <code class="code-pill">new PayeeDao()</code> directly from the Controller and <code class="code-pill">ChangePassword</code> calls <code class="code-pill">/killsession</code> directly via HTTP.</li>
            <li><strong>📌 Viva Follow-Up:</strong> Ask why <code class="code-pill">closeSequelizeConnection()</code> (line 149 of <code class="code-pill">ChangePassword.java</code>) is never called inside <code class="code-pill">run()</code> after <code class="code-pill">sequelize.setAutoclose(false)</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Yamin Aye Card -->
        <div style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-top: 3px solid var(--accent-orange, #f59e0b); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); padding: 1rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <strong style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-primary);">Ma Yamin Aye (2.11.2026)</strong>
            <span class="badge badge-warning">Needs Revision • 62 / 100</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0; line-height: 1.45;">
            <strong>Traced Endpoints:</strong> <code class="code-pill">SaveUserStatus.java</code> &amp; <code class="code-pill">UpdateTransactionStatus.java</code> (both located in <code class="code-pill">ibanking17</code>).
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; line-height: 1.4;">
            <li><strong>&#10003; Good Trace:</strong> Accurately described <code class="code-pill">firsttimelogin=1</code> / <code class="code-pill">Forgot Password</code> flow in <code class="code-pill">SaveUserStatus</code> and async notification in <code class="code-pill">UpdateTransactionStatus</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>&#9888; Issue 1 (Copy-Pasted Routes):</strong> Wrote <code class="code-pill">SaveUserStatus.java (POST /api/addpayee)</code> &amp; <code class="code-pill">UpdateTransactionStatus.java (GET /api/changepassword)</code> — copied Phyo’s routes instead of <code class="code-pill">POST /api/saveuserstatus</code> and <code class="code-pill">POST /api/UpdateTransactionStatus</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>&#9888; Issue 2 (Wrong Repo &amp; Auth):</strong> <code class="code-pill">UpdateTransactionStatus.java</code> is in <code class="code-pill">ibanking17</code> (not <code class="code-pill">admin_console</code>) and has <strong>no auth check</strong>; neither file uses <code class="code-pill">SecurityMiddleware</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>&#9888; Issue 3 (Missing Core Answers):</strong> Omitted <code class="code-pill">@Transactional</code> (Section 3) and did not explain <em>why</em> business logic must never sit in Controller/Repository (Section 5).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick Copy Chat Group Reply -->
      <div style="background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); padding: 0.85rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary);">
            Ready-to-Post Chat Group Review Message
          </strong>
          <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.4rem;" class="no-print">
            <button id="mgr-copy-w5-chat" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;">
              <span>Copy Chat Group Reply</span>
            </button>
            <a href="/milestones/week-5/day-1-review" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;">
              <span>View Full Comparison &amp; Diagrams &rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <textarea
          id="mgr-w5-chat-text"
          rows="8"
          readonly
          style="width: 100%; padding: 0.65rem; background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); color: var(--text-secondary); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.73rem; line-height: 1.45; resize: vertical;"
        >Good effort on Week 5, Day 1 reports, Bro Phyo Min Htet and Sis Yamin Aye! Here is my review of your submissions against the codebase:

@Phyo Min Htet — Approved (92/100 • Strong Codebase Trace)
✅ Great job inspecting the actual source code in both `ibanking17` (`RequestPayeeSetup.java`, `AddPayee.java`) and `admin_console` (`ChangePassword.java`).
✅ Very sharp observation in Section 4 & 5 spotting that `PayeeDao` uses raw JDBC `PreparedStatement` while `UserDao`/`UserHistoryDao` use `Sequelize`, and noticing the architectural anti-pattern where `RequestPayeeSetup` and `AddPayee` call `new PayeeDao()` directly from the Function handler instead of going through `PayeeService`.
📌 Follow-up question for you in chat:
1) Look at `ChangePassword.java` (line 57 & line 149): `sequelize.setAutoclose(false)` is set, and `closeSequelizeConnection()` is defined at the bottom of the class, but is `closeSequelizeConnection()` ever called inside `run()`? What happens to the database connection pool and transaction integrity if `saveUserStatus()` succeeds at line 108 but `saveUserHistory()` fails at line 121?

---

@Yamin Aye — Needs Revision (62/100 • Please Revise & Re-Post in Chat Group)
✅ Good trace of the `firsttimelogin` / `Forgot Password` conditional flow in `SaveUserStatus.java` and the async notification flow (`CompletableFuture.runAsync` -> `SendNotification.sendNoti`) in `UpdateTransactionStatus.java`.
⚠️ However, please fix the following 4 points and re-post your updated sections in the group:
1) Endpoint Route Mix-up (Section 2): You wrote `SaveUserStatus.java (POST /api/addpayee)` and `UpdateTransactionStatus.java (GET /api/changepassword)`. Those routes belong to Phyo Min Htet's endpoints! Check `@FunctionName` and `HttpMethod` in `SaveUserStatus.java` (`POST /api/saveuserstatus`) and `UpdateTransactionStatus.java` (`POST /api/UpdateTransactionStatus`) and write Section 1 & 2 in your own words.
2) Repository Check: Notice that `UpdateTransactionStatus.java` is actually inside `ibanking17` (`com.mit.function`), not `admin_console` (it is a callback endpoint from CAS that calls `otherBankService.updateStatusInAdminConsole`). Please also inspect one true endpoint class inside the `admin_console` project (`com.function.*`).
3) Auth Check on Your Endpoints: Does `SaveUserStatus.java` or `UpdateTransactionStatus.java` actually call `SecurityMiddleware.checkAuth()`? Check whether `UpdateTransactionStatus.java` validates any token at all.
4) Missing Core Questions (Section 3 & 5):
   - Explain the purpose of `@Transactional` boundaries in the Service layer.
   - Explain WHY business logic must never sit inside a Controller or Repository. Look at `SaveUserStatus.java` (lines 118–123 where `BankVendor.NDB` status rules sit in the Function) and `OtherBankService.java` (line 48 where raw SQL `"update accounttransferreport..."` sits inside the Service instead of the DAO) and explain why that violates layered architecture.</textarea>
      </div>
    </div>

